# An inner counter the outer loop does not reset: the store writes 32
# words, 128 B (ptxas unrolls it to 32 stores at param_0 + 0 to 124), its
# base 16 B further on each outer trip. The outer counter steps by the
# inner loop's exit, and the inner one starts from it: 16 (k_out - 1) +
# 4 (k_in - 1). One inner execution touches 16 B.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/carried_counter.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_carried_counter
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 1 sector (ideal 1)  [16 * k[$L__BB0_1] + 4 * k[$L__BB0_2] + param_0 - 20]  k[$L__BB0_2]: +4 B/iter, k[$L__BB0_1]: +16 B/iter
CHECK: global bytes per CTA over the loop's own blocks: requested 512 B, unique 16 B, in sectors 128 B
